  "name": "multi-angle-monologue",
  "description": "Make a one-minute character monologue that plays like a filmed scene: one base still, three more camera angles of the same moment, one voice track with acting tags, the audio cut into parts under 15 seconds at the pauses, each part lip-synced to its own angle with a performance prompt, then an edit that changes angle on every part. Includes the angle prompts, the voice script format with bracketed directions, the per-shot performance prompt, the varg calls and the checks. Use when someone wants a character to deliver a speech, rant, confession, villain monologue, \"explains X in character\" sketch, parody address or documentary-style interview with consistent face and voice for 30 to 90 seconds, or says their talking AI character looks like a frozen avatar. For a remake of an existing scene use scene-recast-video; for the joke and the rules for real people use ai-parody-video; for a two-host show use varg-podcast-video.",
